 #edb/ref 1071 "Select the missing parts in a particular solution of the differential equation ${y}^{″}+36y=f(x),$ where the Fourier series of the $6$-periodic forcing function is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{3(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the free term and all the sine coefficients in the Fourier series of the particular solution are equal to zero.*\n\nThe Fourier series of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-1}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484247 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "88bf7711-bb0b-51a9-9d4e-44874b161912" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484247 #edb/ref 1074 "We assume that a solution of our equation has the following Fourier series:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}))∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}\\frac{n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\ {y}_{p}^{″} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}\\frac{n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}))∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}\\frac{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{9}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{p}^{″}$ and ${y}_{p}$ into the equation and have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}\\frac{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{9}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})+36({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}))={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{3(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\n$$\n\nRearranging the terms to find a common denominator:\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}(36-\\frac{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{9})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{3(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})\n$$\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}(\\frac{324-{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{9})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{3(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\n$$\n\nNow, equating the cosine coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{n}(324-{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2})}{9}=\\frac{3(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}\\,⇒\\,{a}_{n}=\\frac{27(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}(324-{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2})}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{27(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}(324-{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2})}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484314 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3730dcd9-f2ec-50da-be0d-14c755f56a78" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484314 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186317453 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484349 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186484356 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484349 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c1f72d93-f5f8-5ed4-a7c5-2788d86bcace" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484349 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186484247 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484354 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186484314 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484354 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d16e1bd2-5d3a-57fc-8ce5-5535cc365650" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484354 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186397690 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484356 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186484354 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484356 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e1c91699-1134-58dc-ab5b-ea077a7ce0b0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484356 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186317450 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484357 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186484349 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484357 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e69e4c87-91c4-5dd6-a2e7-92fb618add77" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484357 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186484267 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506675 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186507537 #edb/ref 17592186